 "productionNotes": "No source consulted here, Ferrari's own F12tdf release included, gives a production total for the standard F12berlinetta, so productionTotal is null. The only documented figure is for the F12tdf: Ferrari's own October 2015 release says just 799 will be built, and Wikipedia, Hagerty, RM Sotheby's, GTspirit and classic.com all repeat 799, so that number is not in dispute. RM Sotheby's dates the tdf run as built from 2015 through 2017. For the United States, one RM Sotheby's lot describes a 2017 tdf as one of only 299 US-delivery examples, which would be about 37 percent of the run; that is a single auction-house statement and no second source confirms a US allocation, so it is carried at medium confidence. The model years are also worth stating plainly: Car and Driver and Automobile labeled the car a 2013 model in July 2012, Edmunds shows a 2014 model year that carried over unchanged, and classic.com runs the berlinetta from 2013 through 2017. Wikipedia counts the car as produced from 2012 to 2017, which is the European and launch-year count, not the US model-year count. Wikipedia also lists small runs on the same platform: the F60 America at ten examples, the Touring Berlinetta Lusso at five announced, the Superleggera Aero 3 at fifteen and the F12 TRS at two.",
